// Ch12 B05 "The weeping wall" (C, 1 min). K03: a Lit Age retaining wall far older than the pass, drowned
// glimmer seeping out of its joints in thin sheets of cold held light (never frozen: rule 1). P06: the
// Avalanche Ram drinking at the pale pool: still a woolback, three metres at the head, its wool wet and
// matted (ADR 0204 §2: no ice), seep-light showing through the partings; a frayed red herd-cord on its neck.
title: ch12_weeping_wall
location: ch12/keth_pass
---
@letterbox on
@camera K03
// M4-CIN-1304: K03 holds 5 s on the seep before the Ram lifts its head.
@wait 5.0
@camera P06
@anim avalanche_ram lift_head
@music avalanche_ram fade=0.5
Ysolde [cold]: It drank the wrong water. #line:ch12_wall_001
@letterbox off
<<event start_battle ch12_avalanche_ram>>
===
